Phasmid: Web Audio

What:     AudioContext sampleRate, baseLatency, outputLatency and
          destination.maxChannelCount come from the profile's output device;
          the sink opens at those parameters and the audio service resamples.
          Windows profiles get WASAPI's buffer sizing. With audio.noise the
          DynamicsCompressor gain shifts by a few seeded ULPs.
Why:      The host's sink rate, buffer, channel count and playout delay are
          visible to every page and differ by OS.
Profile:  audio.sample_rate, audio.base_latency, audio.output_latency,
          audio.max_channel_count, audio.noise, seed, os.family
Hooks:    content/renderer/media/renderer_webaudiodevice_impl.cc
          GetOutputBufferSize, HandleDeviceStatus, Render;
          third_party/blink/renderer/platform/audio/dynamics_compressor.cc
          constructor, Process; third_party/blink/renderer/platform/BUILD.gn
Contexts: main, iframe, AudioWorklet; workers have no Web Audio
Guard:    tests/guards/audio/webaudio.py

